{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment","id":1103862,"title":"Justice and punishment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-15T11:00:08-07:00","id":1103862,"title":"Justice and punishment","content":"Say that a more pious and law abiding group of werewolvea lived in a city of about 100k mortals, and with only very rare reported wyrm or vampire activity. <br /> A young bone gnawer transforms for the first time, feels threatened by a gang in the city and ends up committing quintuple murderhby-Crinos on their asses. <br /> He is later introduced into the werewolf council and is accepted within the bone gnawer tribe. However, the murders have made the mortals ask allot of unsettlung questions, not to mention they were agents of the local Glass Walkers, the most influential tribe in these parts. <br /> <br /> What would happen to the newly transformed? If you want to be boring you could eityer go &quot;kill him&quot; or &quot;forgive him&quot; and be done with it. But isnt there a more complex scale of punishments? Or, couldnt the glass walkers at least demand some form of retribution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13576-varulv94","name":"Varulv94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T11:41:04-07:00","id":1103869,"title":"","content":"First changes happen and often are messy it's just a fact of life. It's the glass walkers duty to cover up breaches of the veil, they might carry a grudge but a philodox would be quick to point out was their first change any different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 06-15-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T12:54:33-07:00","id":1103884,"title":"","content":"I don't think the cub did anything wrong by Garou standards. Garou aren't going to blame the cub for unintentionally tearing the Veil when he had his First Change.<br /> <br /> Most likely, the sept would simply send the cub to another sept to learn how to be a Garou permanently or for a certain amount of time, and then they'd proceed with whatever they'd have to do to attend to the Veil.<br /> <br /> I do think they would point out the problem of the situation in order to drill it into the cub that this needed to be avoided, and that if done afterwards it would result in some kind of punishment which depending on the severity could include death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:00:35-07:00","id":1103996,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if the Veil was actually threatened. Yes, the claw and teeth marks might be problematic, but most ME would shrug it off and blame it on feral dogs because gang members are not worth the time to figure out the anomalies. Now, if it was a bunch a frat boys going out for some ultraviolence against the homeless (rape and murder), then the ME would be forced to look closely at the deaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:26:41-07:00","id":1104080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varulv94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment#post1103862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say that a more pious and law abiding group of werewolvea lived in a city of about 100k mortals, and with only very rare reported wyrm or vampire activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a city? The vampires might want to stay away for some reason, sure, but Wyrm activity is still going to be fairly high, because it's a city with several dozen thousand people living in it. Not the &quot;unimaginably high&quot; of major metropolitan areas and urban sprawl, but high nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T21:22:31-07:00","id":1104145,"title":"","content":"Wyrm activity will be fairly constant (probably 0.1% of the human population being Fomori). A city that small will likely not get any attention from Pentex, though there may be an Artarkis or two manipulating the city population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T22:21:02-07:00","id":1104160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varulv94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment#post1103862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would happen to the newly transformed? If you want to be boring you could eityer go &quot;kill him&quot; or &quot;forgive him&quot; and be done with it. But isnt there a more complex scale of punishments? Or, couldnt the glass walkers at least demand some form of retribution?</div> </div> </div> </div>How much Power do the Glasswalkers have in the Sept? That's really the important question here while &quot;Officially&quot; most would write it off Garou society is about strength first and foremost if they can force retribution maybe they will, its up to the personalities involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T22:30:25-07:00","id":1104164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment?p=1104160#post1104160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much Power do the Glasswalkers have in the Sept? That's really the important question here while &quot;Officially&quot; most would write it off Garou society is about strength first and foremost if they can force retribution maybe they will, its up to the personalities involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is theirs? Quite a lot. Please remember that before the revised, the basis for the Glass Walkers was the mafia. These wolves have fangs and the lack of empathy to be pretty cruel if they need to be.<br /> <br /> For me, it is the Gnawers and the Coggies who argue for sympathy, much less the Walkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:11:20-07:00","id":1104378,"title":"","content":"In the end most werewolves are going to accept that a new werewolf (even a 'gnawer) is more valuable than a three or four humans. It's unfortunate the newly changed werewolf killed them, but Rage is a fact of life, and a young pup can't really be held responsible for not being able to control himself. If he had been an experienced werewolf and knew what he was and killed some people that might be a different story. But I doubt the caern would agree to any particularly harsh punishment of a young werewolf who had no idea what he was doing. Certainly nothing like executing the poor kid. <br /> <br /> The Glasswalkers might ask that the new Bonegnawer do something useful for them, volunteer or otherwise offer some kind of reparation (nothing too dangerous) and the rest of the caern would go along with it. Ultimately I think the young werewolf would basically be given a stern warning and to let the incident that occurred serve as a powerful lesson for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T12:43:46-07:00","id":1104428,"title":"","content":"I think that the circumstance are also important. If the young Garou was acting in self-defense, I doubt that anyone would argue that the youth was acting in error when they lost control and killed a few people. An experienced Garou is expected to just change to Glabro and beat the punks into a pulp without threatening the Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T07:29:41-07:00","id":1104722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varulv94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment#post1103862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is later introduced into the werewolf council and is accepted within the bone gnawer tribe. However, the murders have made the mortals ask allot of unsettlung questions, not to mention they were agents of the local Glass Walkers, the most influential tribe in these parts.<br /> <br /> What would happen to the newly transformed? If you want to be boring you could eityer go &quot;kill him&quot; or &quot;forgive him&quot; and be done with it. But isnt there a more complex scale of punishments? Or, couldnt the glass walkers at least demand some form of retribution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with statements above mine, the mortals asking questions is a problem that the Glasswalkers or Bone Gnawers will deal with. Send a pack or Cliaths or Fosterns to repair the Veil. If the Glasswalkers do it, it is possible that the BN or the new cub in particular will have to pay some sort of token reparation for the task. Especially with this being the cub's first change, no one is going to blame them for it. The idea of &quot;kill him&quot; should never even be on the table. That would be an absurd reaction from the local Garou. A few human lives are never going to compare in worth to a Garou life.<br /> <br /> Now if the new cub made a habit of rending the Veil, then harsher and harsher punishments would be enacted. But for a first time, absolutely not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:59:02-07:00","id":1104875,"title":"","content":"Ahem.<br /> <br /> &quot;... If you're not a Homid, then you just don't understand, period. You didn't get the luxury of a First Change right in the middle of a crowd of people, most of whom you know by face and name and maybe even personality. And you're among that crowd of people when something little, and it's always the most stupid little thing sets you off. Contrary to the clich\u00e9, you don't 'see red'. You see people, and faces, and your own claws. You know full well whom you killed...&quot; &quot;... Given clothes (one size-fits all outfits), you're given over to a counselor who explains, very patiently that you're not insane, but that yes, you're a monster. It isn't very reassuring, but it's the best procedure we have yet. Meanwhile, all around you people are on phones. And you slowly realize that every single one is talking about you. Think about it for a second. How hard is it to cover up mass murder? It depends upon where you are of course. This whole sequence is mostly true of First World nations... ...And werewolves flipping poorer districts of places like America (I'm talking about Bone Gnawers here) get the advantage that, in general, the police don't care as much... ...But if you're from reasonably wealthy areas, like a large percentage of Glass Walkers, you don't get that advantage. Stopping a police and media investigation of anywhere from six to two dozen murders in one brutal spree is a fiendish process requiring bribes, threats, blackmail and every other edge we can hold over key individuals...&quot; &quot;...And for the second 24 hours, she's slowly watching people she's never laid eyes upon sacrifice their time, money and effort in the pursuit of protecting her. And as they do it, they all have huge grins on their faces; they slap each other's backs and hands and laugh every so often. They're rejoicing, because a cub has been found. If you can get over how horrifying it is, it's absurdly funny.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> Glass Walkers Tribebook. Pages 33-34.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T21:57:39-07:00","id":1104979,"title":"","content":"That seems to be a Glass Walker only problem. The first line is &quot;if you are not a Glass Walker, you do not understand the first 48 hours.&quot; That suggest that Glass Walkers have a unique problem among all of the Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:35:26-07:00","id":1105363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103862-justice-and-punishment?p=1104979#post1104979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be a Glass Walker only problem. The first line is &quot;if you are not a Glass Walker, you do not understand the first 48 hours.&quot; That suggest that Glass Walkers have a unique problem among all of the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just that Glass Walkers have a unique responsibility to protect the veil when homids change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}